                <pb facs="0201" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg141"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Wire the following to our consul at Tientsin: “Carry out at once previous
                    instructions. Insist upon sufficient escort to overcome all real as well as
                    apprehended dangers. Overland route more fatiguing, but demonstration, which
                    China undoubtedly does not favor, is of the utmost importance to us.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
